@startuml

title Geographic IP Hopping - Traffic Flow Analysis

participant "Client Device" as client
participant "Primary Router\n(Entry Point)" as primary
participant "Russia Hop\n(Container)" as russia
participant "Canada Hop\n(Container)" as canada
participant "Taiwan Hop\n(Container)" as taiwan
participant "Australia Hop\n(Container)" as australia
participant "Exit Router\n(SOHO Gateway)" as exit
participant "External Service\n(Destination)" as external

== Initial Connection ==
client -> primary : Connect Request\n(Real IP)
primary -> primary : ZTNA Authentication\nTPM Attestation

== Geographic Hop 1: Russia ==
primary -> russia : WireGuard Tunnel\nEncrypted Payload
note right of russia : Source IP appears as:\n5.101.142.37 (Moscow)\nAS12389 ROSTELECOM

== Geographic Hop 2: Canada ==
russia -> canada : Re-encrypted Payload\nNew WireGuard Tunnel
note right of canada : Source IP appears as:\n174.95.68.145 (Toronto)\nAS812 ROGERS

== Geographic Hop 3: Taiwan ==
canada -> taiwan : Re-encrypted Payload\nNew WireGuard Tunnel
note right of taiwan : Source IP appears as:\n1.160.92.201 (Taipei)\nAS9924 CHUNGHWA

== Geographic Hop 4: Australia ==
taiwan -> australia : Re-encrypted Payload\nNew WireGuard Tunnel
note right of australia : Source IP appears as:\n1.128.156.73 (Sydney)\nAS1221 TELSTRA

== Exit to SOHO Network ==
australia -> exit : Final Encrypted Payload
exit -> exit : Decrypt & Route\nNAT Translation
exit -> external : Request to External Service\n(Appears from Australia)

== Response Path ==
external -> exit : Response Data
exit -> australia : Encrypt & Route Back
australia -> taiwan : Re-encrypt & Forward
taiwan -> canada : Re-encrypt & Forward
canada -> russia : Re-encrypt & Forward
russia -> primary : Re-encrypt & Forward
primary -> client : Decrypt & Deliver

note over client, external
  **Security Benefits:**
  • True client IP never exposed
  • Traffic appears to originate from Australia
  • Multiple encryption layers protect data
  • Geographic diversity confuses traffic analysis
  • Each hop provides independent security validation
end note

note over primary, exit
  **Technical Implementation:**
  • WireGuard tunnels between each hop
  • NAT translation at each geographic point
  • Route table manipulation via OblivionEdge modules
  • Packet monitoring for forensic analysis
  • Automatic failover to backup routes
end note

@enduml